<title>CHINA: Nam Pei Hong posts deeper year loss.</title>
<headline>Nam Pei Hong posts deeper year loss.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   41.8 loss  vs 14.7 loss</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    nil	  vs nil</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  81.58 loss vs 15.09 loss</p>
<p>    Net			    95.66 loss vs 23.13 loss</p>
<p>    Turnover		     123.09     vs 249.45</p>
<p>    Company name		 Nam Pei Hong (Holding) Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  N/A</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   N/A</p>
<p>NOTE - Nam Pei Hong is a Chinese medicine and health food retailer and manufacturer.</p>
<p>Exceptional loss are mainly led by shortfall in inventories, provision for doubtful debts, closure of retail outlets and relocation of operations.</p>
<p>Comparative share earnings figures were adjusted to HK$0.147 from HK$0.149 due to a rights issue of shares during the period. Total dividend for the year is nil vs nil.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
